# tests/run-request-then, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating
# this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST — and it should always have been one: `run-request-then` is a
# WORKER verb, and every fixture here is already a worker. It was a client test
# only because the client was a convenient way to dispatch them and read their
# stdout.
#
# The failure cases are why it looked like it needed a client. They assert that
# an exact-request failure propagates UNCAUGHT, and a worker that lets a run
# fail uncaught dies with it. The answer is that the uncaught path is one level
# down: dispatch a driver that does the uncaught `run-request-then`, and CATCH
# that dispatch. The error text is the proof, and the thing under test is still
# the uncaught path.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --identify:@=identify.sh --driver:@=driver.sh --callback:@=callback.sh --checks:@=checks.sh --boom:@=boom.sh
